# The AI Landscape

#### Let's take a minute to summarize what you learned on the last level!

#### Look at the diagram below to get a better idea of how these terms and concepts fit together. Key terms are defined underneath. 

<p style="text-align:center;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/6360156161735b4ffe0e2f19d74037d4-Screenshot 2024-04-15 at 1.36.49 PM.png" alt="Venn diagram of nested terms related to AI.">

Image Source: https://www.wondavr.com/ai-course/module-1

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Artificial Intelligence (AI):</strong>  AI is the branch of computer science that aims to develop systems capable of performing tasks that would normally require human.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Machine Learning:</strong> a subset of AI that involves training algorithms to learn patterns and make decisions with minimal human intervention, based on data.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Natural Language Processing:</strong> a field at the intersection of computer science, artificial intelligence, and linguistics, focused on enabling computers to understand, interpret, and generate human language.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Deep Learning:</strong> a subset of machine learning that uses neural networks with many layers (deep neural networks) to analyze large volumes of data, enabling the model to learn complex patterns.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Large Language Models (LLMs):</strong> advanced deep learning models trained on extensive corpora of text data, capable of understanding and generating human-like text by predicting subsequent parts of text based on the input they receive.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>ChatGPT:</strong> a prominent example of a large language model, developed by OpenAI, designed specifically for generating human-like responses in a conversational context by processing and producing text based on its training on a diverse dataset.</p>
</div>


#### Everything in this diagram falls under the larger umbrella of Data Science, so let’s define that term too.

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Data Science:</strong> an interdisciplinary field that uses scientific methods, processes, algorithms, and systems to extract knowledge and insights from structured and unstructured data.</p></div>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">I'm not sure I get it...?</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; padding-bottom:20px;">
    <p>

#### It’s okay if you didn’t catch all of that! Here are the same terms defined using non-technical language.

* #### **Artificial Intelligence (AI):** Teaching computers to think and make decisions like humans do.
* #### **Machine Learning (ML):** A way for computers to learn from experience without being directly programmed every step. For example, this is how Netflix recommendation algorithms work.
* #### **Natural Language Processing (NLP):** Helps computers understand and respond to human language, like reading or listening. This is how Siri understands your questions.
* #### **Deep Learning:** A method for computers to learn and make decisions by simulating the network of neurons in a human brain. Used to in facial recognition technology such as unlocking smartphones.
* #### **Large Language Models (LLMs):** Huge computer programs that are really good at understanding and generating human-like text based on what they've learned from a vast amount of written material. The technology behind ChatGPT.
* #### **ChatGPT:** A smart chat program that can write and chat about almost anything by using what it's learned from a lot of books, websites, and other texts.
* #### **Data Science:** The process of finding patterns and answers in a lot of information to help solve problems or make decisions. An example would be how Fitbit and other health trackers to analyze sleep patterns


</p></div>
</details>

